<title>FINLAND: NOKIA WINS FIM 200 MLN GSM ORDER IN HUNGARY.</title>
<headline>NOKIA WINS FIM 200 MLN GSM ORDER IN HUNGARY.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish telecommunications group Nokia Oy said in a statement on Monday it had signed an agreement to supply GSM infrastructure equipment to Hungarian Pannon GSM for over 200 million markka in 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;The contract is the continuation of the co-operation that began in 1993 when Nokia was first chosen to supply a GSM network to Pannon,&quot; it said.  </p>
<p>Pannon -- a consortium of Dutch PTT, Telecom Finland, Tele Denmark, Telenor of Norway and MOL, Antenna Hungaria and Wallis of Hungary -- had over 140,000 subscribers in mid-November, Nokia said.</p>
<p>It said it was the sole supplier for Pannon's GSM network.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358 - 9 - 680 50 242</p>
</text>
